<section class="section partners-page" aria-labelledby="partners-title"><div class="wrap"><div class="partners-intro"><h1 id="partners-title">Help student ideas find their next step.</h1><p class="lead">Abia’s next generation of founders benefits when experienced people, institutions and organisations make room to share what they know.</p></div><div class="partners-body"><div><h2>Build a stronger founder community</h2><p>The Abia Tech Hub Student Startup Incubation Programme is designed to give students practical support as they test an idea and learn how to build a business. Partners can contribute knowledge, time or resources that make this work more useful and grounded.</p></div><div class="partner-contributions"><h2>Ways to contribute</h2><article class="partner-contribution"><span>01</span><div><h3>Share your experience</h3><p>Offer practical guidance to students working through real startup questions.</p></div></article><article class="partner-contribution"><span>02</span><div><h3>Teach a useful skill</h3><p>Lead a focused session that helps founders make progress on a specific challenge.</p></div></article><article class="partner-contribution"><span>03</span><div><h3>Open up resources</h3><p>Help students access tools, spaces or networks that make early experimentation easier.</p></div></article></div></div><div class="partners-next-step"><p>Want to learn more about the programme?</p><a class="btn btn-forest" href="/about">About Abia Tech Hub</a></div></div></section>
